kosha strain

  -- fractional deformation of a material under stress. ε = ΔL/L. dimensionless.
  -- how much does a material deform per unit of its original length?
  -- a 1m steel rod under tension elongates 0.1mm → strain = 0.0001.
  --
  -- elastic strain: remove stress → material returns to original shape.
  -- plastic strain: beyond yield point → permanent deformation remains.
  --
  -- Young's modulus E = σ/ε (within elastic limit).
  -- stiff materials: high E (steel 200 GPa, concrete 30 GPa).
  -- flexible materials: low E (rubber 0.01-0.1 GPa, wood 10 GPa along grain).
  --
  -- Poisson's ratio ν: when a material stretches in one direction,
  -- it contracts in the perpendicular direction. ν = lateral strain / axial strain.
  -- for most metals ν ≈ 0.3. rubber ν ≈ 0.5 (nearly incompressible).

